Subject: maven-core: on OpenVMS, a JDK toolchain finds <tool>.exe

JavaToolchainImpl.findTool() looks for jdkHome/bin/<tool>, adding ".exe"
only on Windows. On OpenVMS the JDK's programs are images too (JAVAC.EXE,
JAVA.EXE), so findTool("javac") returned null for every JDK toolchain:
maven-compiler-plugin warned "Unable to autodetect 'javac' path, using
'javac' from the environment" and compiled with whatever "javac" means
there (on our nodes the JDK Maven runs on), not the toolchain's JDK.

Look for <tool>.exe on OpenVMS as on Windows (plexus-utils' Os family
"openvms"); other systems keep the upstream behaviour.

Fits upstream (apache/maven, maven-core) as an Os family check; to be
offered there.

--- a/vmsport/src/maven-core/org/apache/maven/toolchain/java/JavaToolchainImpl.java	2026-11-11 21:07:24.967589926 +0000
+++ b/vmsport/src/maven-core/org/apache/maven/toolchain/java/JavaToolchainImpl.java	2026-11-11 21:07:25.030447276 +0000
@@ -65,7 +65,9 @@
         File bin = new File(installDir, "bin"); // NOI18N
         if (bin.exists()) {
             boolean isWindows = Os.isFamily("windows"); // NOI18N
-            if (isWindows) {
+            // OpenVMS images are <tool>.EXE too (java.home/bin/java.exe).
+            boolean isOpenVms = Os.isFamily("openvms"); // NOI18N
+            if (isWindows || isOpenVms) {
                 File tool = new File(bin, toolName + ".exe");
                 if (tool.exists()) {
                     return tool;
